NVIDIA Management Library (NVML) C API header, vendored so nvidia_gpu can read GPM-capable GPUs
through NVML + GPM without a CUDA toolkit on the build host (round 2, D28). The monitor never
links libnvidia-ml: src/nvidia_gpu_nvml.c dlopen()s libnvidia-ml.so.1 at runtime (override with
HPCPERFSTATS_NVML_LIB, gated by dyn_lib_path_allowed) and only uses this header for types and
constants.

Source package: cuda-nvml-devel-13-2-13.2.86-1 (NVIDIA CUDA 13.2 repository)
Installed path: /usr/local/cuda-13.2/include/nvml.h
NVML_API_VERSION: 13

File copied unmodified:

  nvml.h  sha256 c3fa30735a7148b9c1019b6b10032001a8833e18a5a891c3ff793db98255829a

Verify:

  echo 'c3fa30735a7148b9c1019b6b10032001a8833e18a5a891c3ff793db98255829a  nvml.h' | sha256sum -c

License: nonexclusive, royalty-free license to use the code in individual and commercial
software (header comment). That license requires the NVIDIA Disclaimer and U.S. Government End
Users Notice from the top of nvml.h to appear in the user documentation and in internal comments
of code that uses it; src/nvidia_gpu_nvml.c carries it, and this README points to it:

  NVML header (c) 1993-2026 NVIDIA Corporation. NVIDIA MAKES NO REPRESENTATION ABOUT THE
  SUITABILITY OF THIS SOURCE CODE FOR ANY PURPOSE. IT IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT EXPRESS OR
  IMPLIED WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. See the full Disclaimer and U.S. Government End Users Notice at
  the top of nvml.h.

Runtime: the GPM APIs (nvmlGpm*) need a driver with GPM support (R520+ on Hopper and newer).
When libnvidia-ml is missing, too old, or any GPU lacks GPM, nvidia_gpu uses the DCGM path.
